   "type": "DOCUMENT",
   "isFreePreview": true,
   "description": "Khung môn học theo syllabus FLM chính thức.",
   "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">TPG203 · Section 0 · Lesson 0.6</span>\n<h2>Student tasks & constructive questions</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">The rules you are held to (attendance, preparation, exam eligibility) — verbatim.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM · Syllabus ID 13864 · Decision 1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT dated 12/12/2025 · collected 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">TPG203 · Mục 0 · Bài 0.6</span>\n<h2>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên & câu hỏi kiến tạo</h2>\n<p class=\"lead\">Những quy định bạn phải tuân theo (chuyên cần, chuẩn bị bài, điều kiện dự thi) — nguyên văn.</p>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: FLM · Syllabus ID 13864 · QĐ 1402/QĐ-ĐHFPT ngày 12/12/2025 · thu ngày 08/11/2026</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student tasks (verbatim)</h3>\n<p>Attend at least 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination<br><br>- Actively participate in class activities<br><br>- Fulfill tasks given by instructor after class<br><br>- Use their own laptop in class only for learning purpose<br><br>- Read the textbook in advance<br><br>- Access the course website (www.cms.fpt.edu.vn) for up-to-date information and material of the course, for online supports from teachers and other students and for practicing and assessment.<br><br>- Complete course's Portfolio with full contents of exercises and submit to the teacher 1 day after the course.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên (nguyên văn)</h3>\n<p>Attend at least 80% of contact hours in order to be accepted to the final examination<br><br>- Actively participate in class activities<br><br>- Fulfill tasks given by instructor after class<br><br>- Use their own laptop in class only for learning purpose<br><br>- Read the textbook in advance<br><br>- Access the course website (www.cms.fpt.edu.vn) for up-to-date information and material of the course, for online supports from teachers and other students and for practicing and assessment.<br><br>- Complete course's Portfolio with full contents of exercises and submit to the teacher 1 day after the course.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions (29)</h3>\n<p>Questions the syllabus asks you to think through before or during the session — try answering them yourself first.</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo (29)</h3>\n<p>Câu hỏi syllabus yêu cầu bạn suy nghĩ trước/trong buổi học — tự trả lời trước khi xem bài.</p></div>\n<table>\n  <thead><tr><th>Session<br><small>Buổi</small></th><th>Code<br><small>Mã</small></th><th>Question (verbatim)<br><small>Câu hỏi (nguyên văn)</small></th></tr></thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr><td>1</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the history of writing development through the stages?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>2</td><td>QN1</td><td>The writing of the Vietnamese people and the world has changed over time. What are those changes? Why did writing evolve?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>3</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the Typography?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>4</td><td>QN1</td><td>Why classify typefaces?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>5</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the difference between a font and typeface?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>6</td><td>QN1</td><td>How many typefaces are there? Analysis of basic typefaces. Give some illustrative examples.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>7</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is spacing around letters?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>8</td><td>QN1</td><td>If the text is playing the role of conveying information and content, what will be the role of typography?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>9</td><td>QN1</td><td>Decipher the difference between Serif and Sans-serif?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>10</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the role of typography in graphic design?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>11</td><td>QN1</td><td>&quot;Serif is more complicated, requiring more stroke and effort than san serif. However, the serif came before the san serif for a period of time. Could you explain why?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>12</td><td>QN1</td><td>Why did writing evolve? Why did languages evolve to be written and read and not just spoken and listened to?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>13</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is the history of a font set development through the stages? (group selection)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>14</td><td>QN1</td><td>Investigate and explore an typeface from the list given below. Choose a theme for your notebook: Futura, Helvetica, Bodoni, Times New Roman, Palatino. What elements of the font create consistency through the font? (group selection)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>15</td><td>QN1</td><td>How many designers built this font set? How? (group selection)</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>16</td><td>QN1</td><td>How does typography affect brand identity design?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>19</td><td>QN1</td><td>Why do different Typefaces deliver different emotions even though they are being used to describe the same context?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>25</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is a magazine?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>26</td><td>QN1</td><td>What types of periodicals and thematic magazines are available on the market today?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>27</td><td>QN1</td><td>How does typography affect magazine design?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>31</td><td>QN1</td><td>Why is it important that you learn the anatomy of typography?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>37</td><td>QN1</td><td>What are the ingredients in the book cover?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>38</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is Drop Cap? How does the word Drop Cap play a role in book design through the stages?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>39</td><td>QN1</td><td>How important are fonts in book cover design? Give some illustrative examples.</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>43</td><td>QN1</td><td>Why is it important that you learn the anatomy of typography?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>49</td><td>QN1</td><td>What is a typography poster?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>50</td><td>QN1</td><td>How does typography affect typography poster design?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>51</td><td>QN1</td><td>In a specific application, why a font must be selected carefully in order to be considered more suitable than others?</td></tr>\n    <tr><td>52</td><td>QN1</td><td>How does Kinetic involve and affect the development of Typography, also with Graphic design?</td></tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Everything in the tables above is copied <strong>verbatim</strong> from the university's FLM page (in English, as published) so you can check it against the copy your lecturer gives you: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13864\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13864</a> (needs your FPT login). If FLM publishes a newer syllabus, FLM wins.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">Mọi thứ trong các bảng trên được chép <strong>nguyên văn</strong> từ trang FLM của trường (bằng tiếng Anh, đúng như trường công bố) để bạn đối chiếu với bản giảng viên phát: <a href=\"https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13864\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">https://flm.fpt.edu.vn/gui/role/student/SyllabusDetails?sylID=13864</a> (cần đăng nhập tài khoản FPT). Nếu FLM công bố bản syllabus mới hơn thì theo FLM.</div></div>"
